<td id="S3.T1.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><math id="S3.T1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{k\in\mathcal{C}}C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">max</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">C</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{k\in\mathcal{C}}C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T1.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T1.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S3.T1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">CBEC</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S3.T1.2.11.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Eq. <a href="#S2.E14" title="In Off-diagonal structure and the CBEC metric. ‣ 2.5 Reliability Diagnostic via Skewness ‣ 2 Per-Class Epistemic Uncertainty ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a></span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Scalar baselines are class-agnostic; per-class variance targets critical classes
via raw <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> but is confounded by <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>
(Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 2.4 (Variance Bound on the Simplex). ‣ 2.3 Why Variance Alone Fails: Boundary Suppression ‣ 2 Per-Class Epistemic Uncertainty ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>); OvA_MI computes binary MI per critical class.
Our three proposed metrics build on <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}C_{k}\approx\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}C_{k}\approx\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math>
(Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 Per-Class Epistemic Uncertainty Vector ‣ 2 Per-Class Epistemic Uncertainty ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>): <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the sharpest
signal when <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> estimates are reliable (<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}&lt;0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}&lt;0.3</annotation></semantics></math>); <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_sum}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_sum</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_sum}}</annotation></semantics></math>
is a smoother alternative; CBEC (Eq. <a href="#S2.E14" title="In Off-diagonal structure and the CBEC metric. ‣ 2.5 Reliability Diagnostic via Skewness ‣ 2 Per-Class Epistemic Uncertainty ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) gates safe–critical pairs
by empirical negative correlation for robustness when skewness degrades <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Results</h3>

<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Theory validation.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before evaluating downstream performance, we verify the additive
decomposition (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2.2 Per-Class Epistemic Uncertainty Vector ‣ 2 Per-Class Epistemic Uncertainty ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>): <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and exact MI achieve Pearson
<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.988" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.988</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.988</annotation></semantics></math> and Spearman <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.998" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.998</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.998</annotation></semantics></math> across all <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7{,}948" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7,948</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7{,}948</annotation></semantics></math> test samples (Figure <a href="#A4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ D.5 Theory Validation: MI vs. ∑_𝑘{𝐶_𝑘} ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>),
confirming the second-order approximation preserves epistemic uncertainty rankings.
The skewness diagnostic (Section <a href="#S2.SS5" title="2.5 Reliability Diagnostic via Skewness ‣ 2 Per-Class Epistemic Uncertainty ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>) shows <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is reliable
(<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}&lt;0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}&lt;0.3</annotation></semantics></math>) for <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{&gt;}94\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>94</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{&gt;}94\%</annotation></semantics></math> of safe-class samples and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="82\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>82</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">82\%</annotation></semantics></math>/<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="63\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>63</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">63\%</annotation></semantics></math> of
Grade 2/3 respectively; full distributions in Appendix <a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Skewness Diagnostic Analysis ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Main results.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Main results. ‣ 3.3 Results ‣ 3 Selective Prediction for Diabetic Retinopathy ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reports AUSC and Critical FNR at 80% coverage with bootstrap CIs.
<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the lowest AUSC (<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.285" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.285</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.285</annotation></semantics></math>), reducing the area under the selective risk curve by 34.7% relative to MI (<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.436" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.436</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.436</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.005" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.005</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.005</annotation></semantics></math>) and by 56.2% relative to Sale_EU_crit (<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.650" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.650</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.650</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.005" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.005</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.005</annotation></semantics></math>).
At the clinically relevant 80% coverage operating point, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves FNR <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.302" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.302</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.302</annotation></semantics></math>, compared to <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.339" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.339</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.339</annotation></semantics></math> for MI and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.409" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.409</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.409</annotation></semantics></math> for Sale_EU_crit.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Selective prediction for DR grading (Bayesian EfficientNet-B4, <math id="S3.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S{=}30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S{=}30</annotation></semantics></math>).
AUSC integrates Critical FNR over all coverages (lower <math id="S3.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math> safer).
<span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bold</span> = best; CIs: 200 bootstrap resamples.</figcaption>
