<section id="A4.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.8 </span>Epistemic Profiles</h3>

<div id="A4.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ D.8 Epistemic Profiles ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> reports the normalised epistemic mass <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[C_{k}/\sum_{j}C_{j}\mid y=i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[C_{k}/\sum_{j}C_{j}\mid y=i]</annotation></semantics></math>, showing which classes absorb epistemic uncertainty for each true label.
Figure <a href="#A4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ D.8 Epistemic Profiles ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> visualises both the raw and normalised profiles as heatmaps.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21160v1/figures/diagnostic_epistemic_profiles.png" id="A4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/150;" width="476" height="150" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Epistemic profiles.
<span id="A4.F6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left:</span> Raw <math id="A4.F6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[C_{k}\mid y{=}i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[C_{k}\mid y{=}i]</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A4.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right:</span> Normalised <math id="A4.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[C_{k}/\sum_{j}C_{j}\mid y{=}i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[C_{k}/\sum_{j}C_{j}\mid y{=}i]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Grade 2 dominates the epistemic budget across all true classes, identifying moderate DR as the model’s primary source of confusion.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Normalised epistemic profiles: <math id="A4.T10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[C_{k}/\sum_{j}C_{j}\mid y{=}i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[C_{k}/\sum_{j}C_{j}\mid y{=}i]</annotation></semantics></math> (Bayesian model).
Each row sums to 100%.
Bold = dominant component.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T10.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T10.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T10.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">True class</th>
<th id="A4.T10.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T10.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T10.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T10.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T10.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T10.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Grade 0</th>
<td id="A4.T10.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">12.3%</td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">32.7%</td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T10.2.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">50.9%</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">4.0%</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T10.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T10.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Grade 1</th>
<td id="A4.T10.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">22.0%</td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">24.8%</td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A4.T10.2.3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">47.1%</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">6.1%</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T10.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T10.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Grade 2</th>
<td id="A4.T10.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A4.T10.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">34.6%</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">18.2%</td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">31.0%</td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">16.2%</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T10.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T10.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Grade 3</th>
<td id="A4.T10.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">21.4%</td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">15.7%</td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T10.2.5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">40.2%</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">22.7%</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Grade 2 is the dominant source of epistemic uncertainty across all true classes, consistent with it being the most confusable category (moderate DR is clinically subtle).
For true Grade 0 and Grade 1, over 50% and 47% of the epistemic mass concentrates on <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, indicating the model’s primary source of doubt about safe-class images is whether they might be moderate DR.
For true Grade 3, the epistemic mass is split between <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (40.2%) and <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> (22.7%), reflecting the severity continuum.
Grade 2 is also the dominant epistemic class (<math id="A4.SS8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max_{k}C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max_{k}C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>) for 64.9% of all test samples, confirming that moderate DR is the model’s primary source of confusion at the individual-input level as well.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.9 </span>Error Signatures</h3>

<div id="A4.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A distinctive advantage of <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{C}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{C}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> over scalar MI is that it fingerprints the <em id="A4.SS9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">structure</em> of model confusion.
Figure <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ D.9 Error Signatures ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[C_{k}\mid y{=}i,\hat{y}{=}j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[C_{k}\mid y{=}i,\hat{y}{=}j]</annotation></semantics></math> for five clinically important outcomes, and Table <a href="#A4.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ D.9 Error Signatures ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> provides the numerical values.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21160v1/figures/paper_error_signatures_bootstrap_bnn.png" id="A4.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/101;" width="476" height="101" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Epistemic signatures of error types.
Each bar shows <math id="A4.F7.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[C_{k}\mid y{=}i,\hat{y}{=}j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[C_{k}\mid y{=}i,\hat{y}{=}j]</annotation></semantics></math> for class <math id="A4.F7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{0,1,2,3\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{0,1,2,3\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Catastrophic misses (<math id="A4.F7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>) and severity errors (<math id="A4.F7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\to 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\to 2</annotation></semantics></math>) have similar MI but distinct <math id="A4.F7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> fingerprints, revealing different confusion pathways invisible to scalar metrics.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.T11" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>Error epistemic signatures: <math id="A4.T11.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[C_{k}\mid y{=}i,\hat{y}{=}j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[C_{k}\mid y{=}i,\hat{y}{=}j]</annotation></semantics></math> for key error types.
Errors with nearly identical scalar MI exhibit strikingly different <math id="A4.T11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> profiles, revealing distinct confusion pathways that suggest different remediation strategies.</figcaption>
