<section id="A4.SS11" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.11 </span>Full Bootstrap Results: MC Dropout</h3>

<div id="A4.SS11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ D.11 Full Bootstrap Results: MC Dropout ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> reports the MC dropout evaluation.
The ranking reversal relative to the BNN (Table <a href="#A4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ D.7 Full Bootstrap Results: Bayesian Model ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) is consistent with both the skewness analysis (Appendix <a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Skewness Diagnostic Analysis ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>) and the findings of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Smith and Gal [2018]</a></cite>, who showed that MC dropout underestimates posterior uncertainty and creates regions of spurious confidence.
The coarser posterior samples inflate <math id="A4.SS11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for critical classes, degrading the reliability of individual <math id="A4.SS11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> values and hence <math id="A4.SS11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math>, while leaving CBEC’s correlation-gated structure intact, since CBEC computes correlations directly from the MC draws rather than relying on the second-order approximation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T13" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span>Full bootstrap results for MC Dropout (<math id="A4.T13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{=}0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{=}0.3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.T13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S{=}30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S{=}30</annotation></semantics></math>, 200 resamples).
CBEC achieves the lowest AUSC, winning 100% of bootstrap samples, while <math id="A4.T13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math> drops to fifth place.
The ranking reversal relative to Table <a href="#A4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ D.7 Full Bootstrap Results: Bayesian Model ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> reflects MC dropout’s inflated skewness for critical classes (Figure <a href="#A4.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Why 𝐶_𝑘 degrades under MC dropout: a skewness analysis. ‣ D.11 Full Bootstrap Results: MC Dropout ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>).</figcaption>
<div id="A4.T13.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:241.5pt;height:78.7pt;vertical-align:-37.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-83.7pt,27.3pt) scale(0.59074231144321,0.59074231144321) ;">
<table id="A4.T13.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
