<th id="A4.T13.2.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">MI</th>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T13.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.425\pm 0.024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.425</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.425\pm 0.024</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T13.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.459\pm 0.019" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.459</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.019</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.459\pm 0.019</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.8.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T13.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.864\pm 0.004" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.864</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.004</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.864\pm 0.004</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T13.2.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T13.2.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Per-class <math id="A4.T13.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T13.2.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A4.T13.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_sum}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_sum</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_sum}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T13.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.436\pm 0.026" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.436</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.026</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.436\pm 0.026</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.9.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T13.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.404\pm 0.017" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.404</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.017</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.404\pm 0.017</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.9.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T13.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.860\pm 0.004" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.860</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.004</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.860\pm 0.004</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T13.2.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T13.2.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Per-class var.</th>
<th id="A4.T13.2.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Sale_EU_crit</th>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T13.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.463\pm 0.027" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.463</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.027</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.463\pm 0.027</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T13.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.527\pm 0.019" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.527</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.019</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.527\pm 0.019</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.10.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T13.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.866\pm 0.004" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.866</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.004</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.866\pm 0.004</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T13.2.1.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T13.2.1.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Per-class MI</th>
<th id="A4.T13.2.1.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">OvA_MI</th>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A4.T13.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.526\pm 0.028" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.526</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.028</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.526\pm 0.028</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.11.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A4.T13.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.556\pm 0.020" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.556</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.020</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.556\pm 0.020</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T13.2.1.11.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A4.T13.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.861\pm 0.004" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.861</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.004</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.861\pm 0.004</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS11.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS11.p2.1" class="ltx_p">CBEC reduces AUSC by 53.6% relative to MI (<math id="A4.SS11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.197" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.197</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.197</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A4.SS11.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.425" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.425</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.425</annotation></semantics></math>) and wins 100% of bootstrap samples.
Scalar entropy (<math id="A4.SS11.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.249" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.249</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.249</annotation></semantics></math>) outperforms all per-class epistemic methods including MI (<math id="A4.SS11.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.425" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.425</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.425</annotation></semantics></math>) under MC dropout; this is because entropy captures total uncertainty (aleatoric + epistemic), and under MC dropout’s coarser posterior, the aleatoric component carries complementary signal that pure epistemic measures miss.
<math id="A4.SS11.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math> still outperforms its unnormalised counterpart Sale_EU_crit (<math id="A4.SS11.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.419" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.419</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.419</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A4.SS11.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.463" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.463</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.463</annotation></semantics></math>), confirming that the <math id="A4.SS11.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> normalisation provides benefit even when the Taylor approximation is degraded.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21160v1/figures/paper_selective_prediction_main_mc_dropout.png" id="A4.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/168;" width="476" height="168" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>MC dropout selective prediction on diabetic retinopathy.
<span id="A4.F9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left:</span> Critical FNR vs. coverage curves. CBEC (orange) dominates at all coverage levels; <math id="A4.F9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math> (red) matches MI at low coverage but diverges at mid-range.
<span id="A4.F9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right:</span> Bootstrap distribution of AUSC (<math id="A4.F9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}200</annotation></semantics></math>). CBEC achieves the lowest AUSC with the tightest spread; <math id="A4.F9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math> and MI are statistically indistinguishable.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Why <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> degrades under MC dropout: a skewness analysis.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A4.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Why 𝐶_𝑘 degrades under MC dropout: a skewness analysis. ‣ D.11 Full Bootstrap Results: MC Dropout ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> reveals the mechanism behind <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s ranking reversal.
Under the low-rank BNN, the fraction of samples with reliable <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}&lt;0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}&lt;0.3</annotation></semantics></math>) remains above <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80\%</annotation></semantics></math> for Grades 0–2 and drops to <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="63\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>63</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">63\%</annotation></semantics></math> only for Grade 3 (Severe/PDR), the rarest and most difficult class.
Under MC dropout, the same statistic degrades monotonically with clinical severity: <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="88\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>88</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">88\%</annotation></semantics></math> (Grade 0), <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="72\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>72</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">72\%</annotation></semantics></math> (Grade 1), <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="54\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>54</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">54\%</annotation></semantics></math> (Grade 2), and only <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="22\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22\%</annotation></semantics></math> (Grade 3).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The right panel quantifies the gap.
Median <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is comparable between the two models at Grade 0 (<math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.013" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.013</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.013</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.012" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.012</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.012</annotation></semantics></math>), where both posteriors are well-behaved.
The gap widens progressively: at Grade 1, MC dropout’s median <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.5\times</annotation></semantics></math> higher than the BNN’s (<math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.130" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.130</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.130</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.037" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.037</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.037</annotation></semantics></math>); at Grade 2 it is <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.1\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.1\times</annotation></semantics></math> higher (<math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.264" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.264</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.264</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.124" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.124</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.124</annotation></semantics></math>); and at Grade 3 the MC dropout median exceeds the reliability boundary entirely (<math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.125" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.125</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.125</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.218" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.218</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.218</annotation></semantics></math>).
For the most safety-critical class, more than three quarters of MC dropout samples operate in the regime where the second-order Taylor approximation has broken down.
This pattern is consistent with MC dropout’s known tendency to underestimate tail variance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Smith and Gal, 2018</a>]</cite>: the resulting predictive distributions are more concentrated than the true posterior, but with heavier skewness, pushing <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> above the reliability threshold precisely for the classes that matter most.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21160v1/figures/appendix_ck_reliability_skewness.png" id="A4.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/177;" width="476" height="177" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span><math id="A4.F10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> reliability comparison: MC dropout vs. low-rank BNN on diabetic retinopathy.
<span id="A4.F10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left:</span> Fraction of test samples with <math id="A4.F10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}&lt;0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}&lt;0.3</annotation></semantics></math> (reliable <math id="A4.F10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>) per DR grade.
The BNN maintains reliability above <math id="A4.F10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60\%</annotation></semantics></math> for all grades; MC dropout drops to <math id="A4.F10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="22\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22\%</annotation></semantics></math> for Grade 3.
Dashed line: <math id="A4.F10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="70\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">70\%</annotation></semantics></math> guide.
<span id="A4.F10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right:</span> Median skewness diagnostic <math id="A4.F10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> per grade.
MC dropout exceeds the <math id="A4.F10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}=0.3</annotation></semantics></math> reliability boundary at Grade 3 (median <math id="A4.F10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.125" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.125</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.125</annotation></semantics></math>), while the BNN remains below it (<math id="A4.F10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.218" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.218</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.218</annotation></semantics></math>).
Critical grades (2, 3) are shaded.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These results provide direct empirical support for the complementarity claimed in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Selective Prediction for Diabetic Retinopathy ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>: <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the preferred deferral metric under well-calibrated posteriors where <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> remains low, while CBEC provides a robust fallback when the posterior approximation inflates skewness beyond the Taylor regime.
The skewness diagnostic <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> therefore serves as a practical model-selection criterion: if median <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for the critical classes exceeds <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.3</annotation></semantics></math>, practitioners should prefer CBEC over <math id="A4.SS11.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS12" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.12 </span>Deep Ensemble Validation: Per-Class Metrics</h3>

<div id="A4.SS12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To verify that the benefit of the <math id="A4.SS12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> normalisation persists across
inference paradigms, we evaluate a deep ensemble of five members on the
same diabetic retinopathy test set (<math id="A4.SS12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7{,}948" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7,948</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7{,}948</annotation></semantics></math> images), using the identical
evaluation pipeline.
Each member shares the Phase 1 EfficientNet-B4 backbone and is fine-tuned
independently with a different random seed; diversity arises from head
initialisation rather than stochastic inference.
We restrict the comparison to MI as the scalar epistemic reference and the
full per-class family: raw per-class variance baselines from
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sale et al. [2024]</a></cite> and our proposed <math id="A4.SS12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> metrics.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reliability.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The deep ensemble achieves near-uniform <math id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> reliability across all DR
grades: <math id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95.7\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95.7</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95.7\%</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="91.2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>91.2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">91.2\%</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="91.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>91.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">91.5\%</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="85.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>85.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">85.1\%</annotation></semantics></math> of samples satisfy
<math id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}&lt;0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}&lt;0.3</annotation></semantics></math> for Grades 0–3 respectively.
This places the ensemble firmly in the high-reliability regime, in
contrast to MC dropout where Grade 3 reliability collapses to <math id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="22\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22\%</annotation></semantics></math>
(Figure <a href="#A4.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Why 𝐶_𝑘 degrades under MC dropout: a skewness analysis. ‣ D.11 Full Bootstrap Results: MC Dropout ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T14" title="Table 14 ‣ Results. ‣ D.12 Deep Ensemble Validation: Per-Class Metrics ‣ Appendix D Diabetic Retinopathy Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> reports AUSC and critical FNR at
<math id="A4.SS12.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80\%</annotation></semantics></math> coverage over 200 bootstrap resamples.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T14" class="ltx_table">
