<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Per-class decomposition (MIMIC-III).</h4>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The binary setting permits direct inspection of per-class contributions: <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}C_{k}=C_{0}+C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}C_{k}=C_{0}+C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Table <a href="#A5.T17" title="Table 17 ‣ Per-class decomposition (MIMIC-III). ‣ E.3 Extended OoD Detection Results ‣ Appendix E OoD Detection Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> reveals that distributional shift affects the two classes asymmetrically.
The survival class exhibits a <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.15\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.15</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.15\times</annotation></semantics></math> increase from ID to OoD (<math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.014\to 0.030" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.014</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0.030</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.014\to 0.030</annotation></semantics></math>), while the mortality class shows only <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.30\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.30</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.30\times</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.022\to 0.029" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.022</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0.029</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.022\to 0.029</annotation></semantics></math>).
The critical-class-only metric <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves AUROC <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.740\pm 0.074" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.740</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.074</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.740\pm 0.074</annotation></semantics></math>, substantially below <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.815\pm 0.017" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.815</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.017</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.815\pm 0.017</annotation></semantics></math>: by focusing exclusively on mortality-class uncertainty, it misses the larger OoD signal carried by <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This illustrates a task-dependent trade-off: <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{crit\_max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>crit_max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{crit\_max}}</annotation></semantics></math> targets safety-critical selective prediction (Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Selective Prediction for Diabetic Retinopathy ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), where critical-class uncertainty directly determines clinical harm; for general OoD detection, all-class aggregation captures the complete distributional shift.</p>
</div>
