</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Per-Class Epistemic Decomposition for FashionMNIST</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main text reports <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> as the best OoD metric for
FashionMNIST<math id="A5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math>KMNIST (AUROC <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.735\pm 0.009" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.735</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.009</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.735\pm 0.009</annotation></semantics></math>) but presents only the
scalar aggregate.
Figure <a href="#A5.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ E.4 Per-Class Epistemic Decomposition for FashionMNIST ‣ Appendix E OoD Detection Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> decomposes this into the ten individual
<math id="A5.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> values, revealing which clothing categories drive the OoD signal
when the model encounters KMNIST inputs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21160v1/figures/fig_perclass_ck_fmnist_vs_kmnist.png" id="A5.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/199;" width="476" height="199" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Per-class epistemic uncertainty <math id="A5.F11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for each of the ten FashionMNIST
categories, comparing ID (FashionMNIST test, <math id="A5.F11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10{,}000</annotation></semantics></math>) vs. OoD
(KMNIST test, <math id="A5.F11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10{,}000</annotation></semantics></math>) samples.
Bars: mean over 5 seeds; error bars: seed standard deviation.
All ten classes show <math id="A5.F11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{C}_{k}^{\text{OoD}}&gt;\bar{C}_{k}^{\text{ID}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mtext>OoD</mtext></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mtext>ID</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{C}_{k}^{\text{OoD}}&gt;\bar{C}_{k}^{\text{ID}}</annotation></semantics></math>, though the magnitude varies considerably
(Bag: <math id="A5.F11.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="18.7\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>18.7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">18.7\times</annotation></semantics></math>; Ankle boot: <math id="A5.F11.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.8\times</annotation></semantics></math>; Table <a href="#A5.T18" title="Table 18 ‣ E.4 Per-Class Epistemic Decomposition for FashionMNIST ‣ Appendix E OoD Detection Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>).
The OoD signal is <em id="A5.F11.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">consistent in direction</em> across all categories
but not uniform in magnitude, suggesting that KMNIST activates some
FashionMNIST class representations more than others.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A5.T18" title="Table 18 ‣ E.4 Per-Class Epistemic Decomposition for FashionMNIST ‣ Appendix E OoD Detection Experiment: Supplementary Details ‣ Not Just How Much, But Where: Decomposing Epistemic Uncertainty into Per-Class Contributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> reports the numerical values for each class.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T18" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 18: </span>Per-class mean <math id="A5.T18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for FashionMNIST (ID) vs. KMNIST (OoD),
averaged over 5 seeds with seed standard deviation.
Ratio <math id="A5.T18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\bar{C}_{k}^{\text{OoD}}/\bar{C}_{k}^{\text{ID}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mtext>OoD</mtext></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mtext>ID</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\bar{C}_{k}^{\text{OoD}}/\bar{C}_{k}^{\text{ID}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
